        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dorothy Parker, Maxine Kumin, John Latouche, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, Leonard Bernstein\n- Works: Candide\n- Roles: poet, author, short story writer, critic, satirist, text contributor\n\nFacts:\n- Dorothy Parker was born on August 22, 1893, and she was an American poet, short story writer, critic, and satirist known for her wit, wisecracks, and eye for 20th-century urban foibles.\n- Maxine Kumin was born on June 6, 1925, and she was an American poet and author.\n- Candide had text contributions from John Latouche, Dorothy Parker, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, and Leonard Bernstein.\n- Dorothy Parker died on June 7, 1967.\n- Maxine Kumin died on February 6, 2014.",
